\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {27}{\ignorespaces Master timeline 2018--2026: Bitcoin price, conventional-asset prices, and the 30-day rolling BTC--S\&P~500 correlation, with all eleven landmark events marked. Red dotted lines~=~crash/shock events; green~=~rallies and all-time highs; blue~=~structural divergences; purple~=~institutional milestones.}}{64}{figure.caption.49}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {28}{\ignorespaces Correlation regime map. Left: post-event BTC correlation (30-day average) with each conventional asset. Right: change in correlation relative to the 30-day pre-event average. Red/blue = strong positive/negative shifts.}}{65}{figure.caption.51}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {29}{\ignorespaces \textbf {Event 1 --- COVID Black Thursday (12 March 2020).} Bitcoin fell $\sim \!50\%$ in 24 hours, sharply outpacing equity losses. The 30-day BTC--S\&P~500 correlation spiked from near zero to above 0.70 --- a liquidity-driven sell-off in which Bitcoin's diversification benefit temporarily disappeared. Source: \href {https://www.reuters.com/article/us-health-coronavirus-markets-idUSKBN20Z0TO}{Reuters}}}{66}{figure.caption.53}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {30}{\ignorespaces \textbf {Event 2 --- FTX Collapse (8--11 November 2022).} SBF's exchange filed for bankruptcy; Bitcoin fell 26\% over 72 hours. Paradoxically the S\&P~500 \emph {rose} 5\% the same week on a positive CPI print --- producing a brief but striking negative BTC--equity correlation. Source: \href {https://www.bbc.com/news/technology-63631492}{BBC News}}}{66}{figure.caption.54}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {31}{\ignorespaces \textbf {Event 3 --- SVB Banking Crisis (10 March 2023).} Silicon Valley Bank's failure triggered a 30\% Bitcoin rally as investors sought alternatives to the banking system. Both Bitcoin and Gold rose while equities fell --- one of the rare episodes in the sample where the 30-day BTC--S\&P~500 correlation flipped to strongly negative. Source: \href {https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/10/business/silicon-valley-bank-failure-explained.html}{The New York Times}}}{67}{figure.caption.55}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {32}{\ignorespaces \textbf {Event 4 --- ``Liberation Day'' Tariff Shock (2 April 2025).} Sweeping tariffs on 185 countries caused the S\&P~500 to fall 10\% in four trading days --- its fastest drop since March 2020. Bitcoin fell 18\% alongside equities; Gold surged to above \$3\,200/oz. This episode produced the highest single-event BTC--S\&P~500 correlation spike in the dataset ($\rho > 0.80$) and illustrates most clearly that Bitcoin behaves as a risk asset, not a safe haven, during macro shocks. Source: \href {https://www.reuters.com/markets/trump-liberation-day-tariffs-global-markets-crash-2025-04-02/}{Reuters}}}{67}{figure.caption.56}%
